    "created_at": "2020-03-10T17:03:20Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-03-10T17:03:20Z",
    "body": "Also, I thought whatwg was focused on describing what browsers implement instead of theoretical purity.  The reality is that browsers have implemented the distinction between content-set headers and browser-set headers when it comes to CORS preflights for a long time.  We ran into a lot of compat pain when we tried to remove the distinction in order to conform strictly to the current spec text.",
